00:15:09,220 --> 00:15:10,500
Ah, shiiiit!

261
00:15:23,780 --> 00:15:24,610
Weather!

262
00:15:26,540 --> 00:15:27,620
We're melting!

263
00:15:27,940 --> 00:15:29,705
What the hell is this weather?

264
00:15:29,860 --> 00:15:30,820
All right!

265
00:15:30,940 --> 00:15:32,597
The big bad wolf is gonna drown today!

266
00:15:32,680 --> 00:15:35,420
Just like the star of you! Hooray!

267
00:15:36,800 --> 00:15:37,630
It's over.

268
00:15:37,713 --> 00:15:38,980
Just as it should be.

269
00:15:39,440 --> 00:15:43,322
I shall honor your sacrifice by
living a happy life in your stead.

270
00:15:44,480 --> 00:15:45,697
According to experts,

271
00:15:45,780 --> 00:15:47,597
the countries with the
most damages from this

272
00:15:47,680 --> 00:15:49,617
fantasy hero incident
are the United States...

273
00:15:49,700 --> 00:15:51,935
What can I do for you, Master Aladdin?

274
00:15:52,720 --> 00:15:55,720
Since you freed me, I will
be your devoted servant.

275
00:15:56,080 --> 00:15:57,157
With my power I can...

276
00:15:57,240 --> 00:15:59,880
Stop mumbling to
yourself, you little brat!

277
00:16:01,800 --> 00:16:03,741
Give me that book you're reading.

278
00:16:03,840 --> 00:16:04,670
What is this?

279
00:16:07,160 --> 00:16:07,990
I...

280
00:16:08,073 --> 00:16:08,903
I can't breathe.

281
00:16:08,986 --> 00:16:12,760
What more could you want from
me? Nothing. This is fine.

282
00:16:13,180 --> 00:16:14,800
You've done well, thanks.

283
00:16:15,200 --> 00:16:17,200
You're a really talented artist.

284
00:16:18,320 --> 00:16:20,920
What did you make him draw? Hallweather?

285
00:16:21,680 --> 00:16:26,180
I had Van Gogh here put his skills
to work and create a hero for me.

286
00:16:26,560 --> 00:16:27,957
They have a story too.

287
00:16:28,040 --> 00:16:31,240
Like most heroes, they have powers!

288
00:16:31,660 --> 00:16:35,778
The power to defeat fantasy heroes
and return them all back to normal!

289
00:16:45,780 --> 00:16:48,300
And this story can only end one way!

290
00:16:48,620 --> 00:16:51,561
With the hero bringing
everything back to reality!

291
00:16:54,540 --> 00:16:57,700
We're gonna return just
like the story describes!

292
00:16:58,040 --> 00:17:00,200
Anastasia, there's no need to worry.

293
00:17:00,420 --> 00:17:03,008
We're gonna return to
our bodies and hearts.

294
00:17:09,900 --> 00:17:11,680
Hey, I said hey.

295
00:17:12,520 --> 00:17:14,800
Come on, give me back my book.

296
00:17:15,680 --> 00:17:17,386
Coming to you with an update.

297
00:17:17,700 --> 00:17:20,257
It appears everything has
suddenly returned to normal.

298
00:17:20,340 --> 00:17:23,917
All picture books, paintings,
comics, and films have been restored.

299
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:28,700
Mona Lisa, Snow White, Batman, and
even Tweety Bird have all returned.

300
00:17:29,080 --> 00:17:33,962
Yet we have received reports that Pinocchio
has not reverted to its original place.

301
00:17:34,080 --> 00:17:34,962
Are you asleep?

302
00:17:35,360 --> 00:17:36,520
Was it too boring?

303
00:17:37,080 --> 00:17:38,433
I don't see how though.

304
00:17:38,660 --> 00:17:40,836
The story is so full of hope and fun.

305
00:17:52,200 --> 00:17:55,200
Hey, what car are you
driving around in these days?

306
00:17:57,240 --> 00:17:58,480
You get a new one?

307
00:17:58,680 --> 00:18:01,798
You aren't driving the same
car from before, are you?

308
00:18:01,960 --> 00:18:02,790
Romeo?

309
00:18:04,300 --> 00:18:05,130
Jolene!

310
00:18:05,400 --> 00:18:06,960
Just help me, Jolene!

311
00:18:07,140 --> 00:18:09,137
Have you ever heard of
plea bargaining before?

312
00:18:09,220 --> 00:18:13,620
Defendant Jolene Kujo is
sentenced to 15 years in... ROMEO!

313
00:18:15,020 --> 00:18:17,620
Wait, I thought you were... But how?

314
00:18:18,120 --> 00:18:19,660
Make this easy, Romeo.

315
00:18:20,100 --> 00:18:22,041
Don't go anywhere near the phone.

316
00:18:22,420 --> 00:18:23,980
Any phone for that matter.

317
00:18:24,280 --> 00:18:25,280
Am I clear?

318
00:18:25,840 --> 00:18:27,937
I would never do something like that.

319
00:18:28,020 --> 00:18:31,138
Ever since that day, I've
been regretting what I did.

320
00:18:31,340 --> 00:18:34,197
I can't forgive the sin
I've committed against you.

321
00:18:34,280 --> 00:18:38,580
After losing you the way I did, I
finally realized just how stupid I was.

322
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:43,680
Jolene, I swear to God, I'm
so sorry for betraying you.

323
00:18:43,940 --> 00:18:45,469
How will you ever forgive?

324
00:18:45,840 --> 00:18:46,900
Shh, shh.

325
00:18:47,140 --> 00:18:49,480
You don't have to say a word, Romeo.

326
00:18:52,700 --> 00:18:54,977
You're the only one in this world for me.

327
00:18:55,060 --> 00:18:55,890
I see it now.

328
00:18:55,973 --> 00:18:57,480
It has to be you, baby.

329
00:18:58,260 --> 00:19:01,860
I tried to visit you in jail,
too, but they didn't let me.

330
00:19:03,700 --> 00:19:04,530
Oh, Romeo.

331
00:19:04,880 --> 00:19:06,137
Poor, poor Romeo.

332
00:19:06,220 --> 00:19:08,280
Have you always been this pitiful?

333
00:19:09,760 --> 00:19:12,117
Listen, just forget about the hit-and-run.

334
00:19:12,200 --> 00:19:13,965
I don't care about it anymore.

335
00:19:14,240 --> 00:19:17,060
I don't hate you, and
I don't hold a grudge,

336
00:19:17,280 --> 00:19:20,809
now that I know the wreck was
all part of a plot against me.

337
00:19:21,940 --> 00:19:25,293
Romeo, I came here because I
need to ask you for a favor.

338
00:19:26,380 --> 00:19:28,117
I want some money and a car.

339
00:19:28,200 --> 00:19:30,612
There is an important place I need to be.

340
00:19:33,840 --> 00:19:36,311
Yeah, sure, but I only have a grand on me.

341
00:19:37,180 --> 00:19:40,040
And here, these are my
keys. This is plenty.

342
00:19:40,360 --> 00:19:41,460
Thank you, Romeo.

343
00:19:41,960 --> 00:19:46,740
But if the police come by, don't
say anything. Promise me. Oh, man.

344
00:19:47,080 --> 00:19:51,845
Jolene, I plan on turning myself in so
that I can prove you were always innocent.

345
00:19:52,020 --> 00:19:54,200
So please, come back to me!

346
00:20:08,620 --> 00:20:10,337
Awesome you got the keys to his car?

347
00:20:10,420 --> 00:20:15,480
Hello yes my name is Romeo
Jazz and I live in Palm Beach.

348
00:20:15,980 --> 00:20:17,017
Is this the police?

349
00:20:17,100 --> 00:20:19,637
I'd like to report an escaped convict.

350
00:20:19,720 --> 00:20:22,960
Yes her name is Jolene Cujo.

351
00:20:24,500 --> 00:20:25,460
Like I thought.

352
00:20:25,760 --> 00:20:27,477
Aren't you glad I told
you to plant one of my

353
00:20:27,560 --> 00:20:29,957
stickers on that bendejo
and split it in two?

354
00:20:30,040 --> 00:20:31,920
He's already calling the cops.

355
00:20:32,100 --> 00:20:33,020
That snitch.

356
00:20:34,120 --> 00:20:34,950
No!

357
00:20:35,033 --> 00:20:35,863
You're mistaken.

358
00:20:35,946 --> 00:20:36,857
She never came to my house.

359
00:20:36,940 --> 00:20:37,999
She couldn't have.

360
00:20:38,300 --> 00:20:42,124
I'm calling in to report because
I just received a call from her.

361
00:20:42,460 --> 00:20:43,401
Yes, that's all.

362
00:20:43,720 --> 00:20:46,597
She was begging for money,
but I turned her down.

363
00:20:46,680 --> 00:20:49,209
I think she said she
was headed for Mexico.

364
00:20:49,920 --> 00:20:50,750
Of course.

365
00:20:51,120 --> 00:20:53,355
If she calls again, I'll let you know.

366
00:20:54,380 --> 00:20:55,480
Yes, goodbye.

367
00:20:56,440 --> 00:20:57,852
Well damn, look at that.

368
00:20:58,080 --> 00:21:00,100
He didn't betray you after all.

369
00:21:00,760 --> 00:21:02,936
If only she could forgive me one day.

370
00:21:03,020 --> 00:21:04,580
I'd do anything for her.

371
00:21:07,360 --> 00:21:08,617
Hey, check it out!

372
00:21:08,700 --> 00:21:09,660
Isn't it cool?

373
00:21:09,840 --> 00:21:10,900
Your ex is loaded!

374
00:21:11,400 --> 00:21:12,917
What do you think he gave you?

375
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:15,765
Sure his car keys are
here, but that's not all.

376
00:21:16,200 --> 00:21:17,440
Look at that thing!

377
00:21:21,160 --> 00:21:23,197
Are we really allowed to take that one?

378
00:21:23,280 --> 00:21:24,897
I want to try steering.

379
00:21:24,980 --> 00:21:29,840
Flying the real thing must be Way different
from just reading about it in books.

380
00:21:32,580 --> 00:21:34,057
Romeo, you've changed.

381
00:21:34,140 --> 00:21:35,580
I believe you.

382
00:21:38,820 --> 00:21:40,477
But let's peel it off anyway.

383
00:21:40,560 --> 00:21:42,080
Just in case.

384
00:21:47,520 --> 00:21:48,840
Let's get out of here.

385
00:21:49,180 --> 00:21:52,651
If we take the helicopter, we
can get there in a few hours.

386
00:22:04,080 --> 00:22:07,500
Although you think I cope

387
00:22:08,920 --> 00:22:12,697
My head is filled with hope

388
00:22:12,780 --> 00:22:17,077
Of some place

389
00:22:17,160 --> 00:22:20,780
other than here

390
00:22:23,520 --> 00:22:27,160
Although you think I smile

391
00:22:28,760 --> 00:22:32,300
Inside and all the while

392
00:22:34,040 --> 00:22:40,400
I'm wondering about my destiny?

393
00:22:42,980 --> 00:22:44,897
I'm thinking

394
00:22:44,980 --> 00:22:50,577
about all the

395
00:22:50,660 --> 00:22:55,457
things I'd like

396
00:22:55,540 --> 00:23:01,480
to do in my life.

397
00:23:03,380 --> 00:23:06,717
I'm a dreamer,

398
00:23:06,800 --> 00:23:11,580
a distant dreamer,

399
00:23:13,460 --> 00:23:15,237
dreaming for

400
00:23:15,320 --> 00:23:21,520
all from today.

401
00:23:25,660 --> 00:23:29,560
Father, I understand that my
mission will be protecting you,

402
00:23:30,700 --> 00:23:33,680
But before that, will
you please open my eyes?

403
00:23:34,060 --> 00:23:35,620
You see one of my eyelids.

404
00:23:36,020 --> 00:23:40,100
It keeps on drooping down,
and it doesn't go back up.

405
00:23:41,240 --> 00:23:43,400
It only goes up sometimes.

406
00:23:59,560 --> 00:24:00,390
Thank you.

407
00:24:38,340 --> 00:24:39,700
Thank you.
